I read the original post (http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/
wishirl.html), and they mentioned some bad things about artifacts and
spells. Intellifacts blast crossaligned users, and spells are
difficult to learn/cast at best. Keeping that in mind, I believe most
humans would be Neutral, but criminals and law-enforcers would
probably be their respective alignments. (This is a little sketchy to
define, though, and any opinions are welcome.)

I'll stick the speed part here:

"Speed boots make you 2/3 faster than normal. This could mean that
they reduce your lifespan, making you "live fast, die young", but then
nobody would consider them worth wishing for. So I'll assume that it
means that you live 5 subjective hours for every 3 hours that pass in
the outside world, you still need to spend 1/3 of your time asleep,
and your objective lifespan is not reduced by this acceleration. (I'm
also ignoring the problem of getting out of phase with the world if
you are asleep for 8 subjective hours and awake for 16.) This means
that you get 16*2/3 = 10 2/3 extra (subjective) hours awake every
(objective) day."

A blessed tin of orange dragon meat might be a better wish for those
not wanting to screw around with temporal issues.

"If Earth is considered to be one huge level, a blessed scroll of
magic mapping or gold detection, or a potion of object detection."
That's another good consideration :D

Personally, I'd go with the orange dragon meat, as I love the night,
and hate sleeping.

